Recommends: gnome-settings-daemon, gnome-shell
Description: switch inputs, screen layouts and KVM on DDC/CI monitors
 A GTK 4 / libadwaita application and command line tool that controls
 monitors over DDC/CI:
 .
  * select the active video input
  * choose the screen layout: single input, side by side in several
    splits, or picture in picture; swap sides and pick the second input
  * hand the monitor's built-in KVM (USB hub with keyboard and mouse)
    to the other computer
  * brightness, contrast and speaker volume
  * optional system-wide GNOME keyboard shortcuts
 .
 A GNOME Shell extension adds a Monitor tile to Quick Settings, shows
 GNOME's on-screen pop-up for shortcut actions and can hand over the
 keyboard and mouse when the pointer is pushed against the screen edge
 next to the other computer.
 .
 Developed and tested with a U4025QW monitor; manufacturer-specific VCP
 codes are configurable for other models.
